'stem-chateau-badette|2012':{blend:{ME:90,CF:7,PV:3},src:'Chateau-Badette-2012-FR.pdf',alc:13.5,oak:30,ph:3.7,yld:45},
'stem-chateau-badette|2013':{blend:{ME:85,CF:10,PV:5},src:'Chateau-Badette-2013-FR.pdf',alc:14,oak:30,ph:3.55,yld:45},
'stem-chateau-badette|2014':{blend:{ME:85,CF:12,PV:3},src:'Chateau-Badette-2014-FR.pdf',alc:14.5,oak:30,ph:3.62,yld:45},
'stem-chateau-badette|2015':{blend:{ME:90,CF:7,PV:3},oak:100,src:'Chateau-Badette-2015-FR.pdf',note:'After a hot, dry spring, the summer was particularly sunny, with marked water stress which favoured concentration and richness. The rains in August allowed the grapes to ripen again without being diluted excessively, while September and October were dry and moderately warm, providing an ideal window of opportunity for a calm, spread-out harvest. The red wines have excellent density, generous aromatic expression, ripe, silky tannins and excellent ageing potential. A complete vintage, combining power, elegance and balance. This cuvée has a dark, intense colour, heralding a wine of great concentration.',alc:16,months:'18',ph:3.71,yld:45},
'stem-chateau-badette|2016':{blend:{ME:85,CF:10,PV:5},src:'Chateau-Badette-2016-FR.pdf',alc:15.5,oak:85,ph:3.5,yld:45},
'stem-chateau-badette|2017':{blend:{ME:85,CF:10,PV:5},oak:80,src:'Chateau-Badette-2017-FR.pdf',alc:15,months:'12',ph:3.61,yld:45,wy:[2022,2034]},
'stem-chateau-badette|2018':{blend:{ME:85,CF:10,PV:5},oak:50,src:'Chateau-Badette-2018-FR.pdf',alc:14.5,months:'18',ph:3.54,yld:45},
'stem-chateau-badette|2019':{blend:{ME:80,CF:15,PV:5},src:'Chateau-Badette-2019-FR.pdf',alc:15,oak:50,ph:3.54,yld:45},
'stem-chateau-badette|2020':{blend:{ME:80,CF:15,PV:5},oak:80,src:'Chateau-Badette-2020-FR.pdf',note:'The growing cycle was early, with budbreak and flowering advancing under summer-like conditions as early as spring. The hot, dry summer encouraged rapid ripening, with varying levels of water stress depending on the terroir. Harvesting began in late August for the white varieties (which showed excellent sanitary conditions), followed by the Merlots in early September under fair weather. The Cabernets were sometimes picked quickly at the end of September ahead of Storm Alex. The red wines are structured, dense, and well-balanced: Merlots are fruity, deeply colored, and flavorful, while Cabernets are intense and fresh without excessive greenness. It is a remarkable success for early-ripening terroirs, offering harmony and excellent ageing potential.',alc:15,months:'16',ph:3.62,yld:45,wy:[2023,2042]},
'stem-chateau-badette|2021':{blend:{ME:80,CF:15,PV:5},oak:25,src:'Chateau-Badette-2021-FR.pdf',alc:14.5,ph:3.56,pick:{ALL:'10-08|'},yld:45},
'stem-chateau-badette|2023':{blend:{ME:75,CF:20,PV:5},oak:34,src:'Chateau-Badette-2023-FR.pdf',note:'2023 in Bordeaux was marked by contrasting weather conditions, requiring a high level of responsiveness in the vineyards. Moderate budburst prevented frosts, but very high downy mildew pressure had a variable impact on the vineyards, depending on the terroirs and practices.Flowering was rapid and uniform, and took place under good conditions. Despite a staggered veraison, the summer, punctuated by thunderstorms and a scorching late August, favoured regular ripening, while keeping the grapes fresh.The harvest benefited from a favourable late season. The Merlots are charming and expressive. The nose has a toasty character, with controlled richness, freshness and good aromatic definition.',alc:15.5,months:'18',ph:3.64,yld:45,wy:[2029,2046]},
'stem-chateau-badette|2024':{blend:{ME:75,CF:20,PV:5},src:'Chateau-Badette-2024-FR.pdf',oak:40,ph:3.49,yld:45},
'stem-chateau-badette|2025':{blend:{ME:75,CF:20,PV:5},oak:40,src:'Chateau-Badette-2025-FR.pdf',alc:14.5,months:'18',yld:45,wy:[2029,2050]},
'artisan-chateau-de-lauga|2019':{blend:{CS:55,ME:40,PV:4,CA:1},months:'12',oak:10,press:{'Decanter':'89','James Suckling':'89'},src:'Fiche-technique-LAUGA-ENG.pdf'},
'bourgeois-chateau-beauvillage|2017':{blend:{CS:45,ME:55},alc:13,months:'12',src:'Fiche-technique-Chateau-Beauvillage-millesime-2017.pdf',taste:'Belle robe rouge bordeaux, brillante. Le premier nez est friand, gourmand. Les notes de petits fruits rouges et bleus sont présents, aromes de groseille et de myrtille. Belle complexité à l’aération avec des notes toastées, le boisé est bien intégré, fondu. La bouche est bien construite, les tanins sont enrobés par une belle sucrosité. Il y a également beaucoup de fraîcheur, une belle acidité qui apporte de la longueur. Finale gourmande sur des notes de fruits rouges.'},
