'bourgeois-chateau-moulin-de-canhaut|2015':{yld:47,months:'8',src:'INSULA-AMPHORA-2015.pdf',note:'2015 is a synergy of two exceptional vintages, 2005 and 2010. Nature gave us optimal weather throughout the vine\'s cycle, which allowed us to harvest all our plots at full ripeness. This vintage gives wines of a great aromatic richness, with a tannic weave.'},
'bourgeois-chateau-moulin-de-canhaut|2018':{yld:47,src:'Insula-amphora-2018-anglais.pdf',food:'INSULA "Amphora" offers a new journey for wine amateurs. This wine is slightly more oncentrated in natural antioxidants and reveals all the expression of mature fruits. We can appreciate it from aperitif, but also on slowly cooked dishes like a "Lamb\'s shoulder".'},
'bourgeois-chateau-moulin-de-canhaut|2021':{yld:45.5,months:'12',src:'MOULIN-DE-CANHAUT-2021.pdf'},
'bourgeois-chateau-moulin-de-canhaut|2022':{yld:45.5,months:'12',src:'MOULIN-DE-CANHAUT-2022.pdf'},
'bourgeois-chateau-patache-d-aux|2018':{alc:14,yld:36,months:'12',press:{'James Suckling':'91','Jancis Robinson':'16.5','Vinous':'90'},src:'Chateau-Patache-dAux-Medoc-Cru-Bourgeois-2018-FR.pdf',note:'2018 allowed us to harvest our Cabernet Sauvignons at a very fine tannic ripeness. Tasted today, it is a very structured wine, wholly characteristic of its northern Médoc terroir. A deep purple colour. On the nose the aromatics are marked by black fruit, by empyreumatic notes brought by the Cabernets, and by floral notes typical of ripe Merlots on limestone soils. On the palate the tannin is beginning to melt with the oak. The density is impressive and deserves to be tamed, so complex, delicate and many-sided does the wine show itself once opened.',pick:{ALL:'09-20|10-17'}},
'bourgeois-chateau-poitevin|2016':{yld:47,months:'4',src:'CHATEAU-POITEVIN-2016-ANGLAIS.pdf',food:'Château Poitevin will pair nicely with some recipes made from red meats, stewed­meat, duck confit, game, bordelaise­style lamprey, funghi porcini mushrooms, fresh pasta with truffles, and of course with many cheeses like Camembert, Brie, Saint­Nectaire, Maroilles, Comté.'},
'bourgeois-chateau-poitevin|2023':{note:'2023 at Château Poitevin was marked by a kind spring followed by a warm, humid summer, giving contrasting weather. Although the volume harvested was smaller than usual, that reduction brought about a concentration of aromas in the berries. Despite the challenges, our team kept the vines healthy, guaranteeing the quality of the grapes picked. We look forward to discovering the unique expression of this vintage.'},
'bourgeois-chateau-prieure-de-beyzac|2022':{press:{'Neal Martin':'91'},src:'SELECTION-CEBA-CADEAUX-DAFFAIRES-2022-Chateau-Prieure-de-Beyzac.pdf',oak:25},
'dalem|2018':{yld:40,months:'18',oak:40,src:'Technical-Sheet-Chateau-Dalem-2018-angl.pdf.pdf'},
'dalem|2019':{yld:40,months:'18',oak:40,src:'Technical-Sheet-Chateau-Dalem-2019-angl.pdf.pdf'},
'dalem|2020':{yld:40,months:'18',oak:50,src:'Technical-Sheet-Chateau-Dalem-2020-angl.pdf.pdf'},
'dalem|2023':{blend:{ME:85,CF:14,MA:1},yld:35,months:'18',oak:50,src:'FT-Primeur-2023-DALEM-.pdf'},
'dalem|2024':{blend:{ME:90,CF:9,MA:1},yld:13,months:'18',oak:40,src:'FT-Primeur-2024-DALEM.pdf',note:'2024 follows the same line as 2023, marked by a level of permanent struggle against the hazards of the weather and the other pests of the vine. The weather set upon the Bordeaux vineyard relentlessly, with the exception of a saving summer truce, pushing us to show resilience and invention. In a complicated climate the 2024 vintage managed to assert itself against adversity and bring forth wines of a great finesse and a great freshness. It will not be an opulent vintage like 2022, but it will be a vintage of terroir and of the grower. These cooler Bordeaux vintages, more to the taste of today\'s drinkers, are probably the ones in which the finest discoveries are made. The depth of colour is remarkable.'},
