'de-fieuzal|2010':{blend:{CS:70,ME:15,PV:15},src:'de-fieuzal-2010-021a24a4.pdf',note:'After a patch of uneven weather between the bud break and the flowering, the climate was pleasantly dry and warm during the grapes\' early ripening phases. A few damp days at the beginning of September were a blessing for the white wine grapes. This brief wet spell was followed by a perfect Indian summer which allowed us to harvest the grapes in perfect condition. Château de Fieuzal 2010 is a generous, rich wine. It is both supple and distinguished, with a perfectly precise acidity that provides a classic balance to the wine\'s fruit flavours. Notes of blackcurrant, blackberry and violet dominate the aromas, but there are also hints of tobacco and spices with a slight touch of pepper. Without doubt this is due to the predominance of cabernet sauvignon in the blend, which is beautifully matched to a smaller percentage of impeccable petit-verdot. This wine, which is the result of historically low harvest volumes, has the capacity to evolve into something truly special. All in all an incomparable vintage.'},
'la-violette|2025':{blend:{ME:80,CF:20},months:'12',oak:27,src:'la-violette-2025-cc00f818.pdf',taste:'Le nez, complexe et frais, révèle violette, fruits rouges et une touche graphite. La bouche est dense et pleine dès l’attaque, portée par des tannins charnus et soyeux. Le cabernet franc allonge la trame et conduit à une longue finale élégante et harmonieuse. Ce millésime 2025 se distingue par sa puissance maîtrisée, son équilibre raffiné et sa grande expression aromatique. TASTING NOTE The nose, complex and fresh, reveals violet, red fruit, and a touch of graphite. The palate is dense and full from the attack, supported by fleshy and silky tannins. The Cabernet Franc lengthens the structure and leads to a long, elegant, and harmonious finish. This 2025 vintage is distinguished by its controlled power, refined balance, and great aromatic expression. SUPERFICIE EN PRODUCTION 13,70 Ha NATURE DES SOLS Un terroir exceptionnel avec un sous-sol de molasses du Fronsadais et d’argiles sableuses vertes, recouvertes par des colluvions sableux brunifiés. DENSITÉ DE PLANTATION 6 060 et 6 700 pieds/Ha ENVIRONNEMENT HVE 3. Produits bio et biocontrôle privilégiés, pas de CMR. Confusion sexuelle. Enherbement raisonné, semis temporaires selon la vigueur de la parcelle. TRAVAUX DU VIGNOBLE Labours traditionnels, désherbage mécanique. Ébourgeonnage manuel, épamprage, effeuillage, échardage. Élimination des grappes à grains de maturité hétérogène à partir de mi-véraison si nécessaire.'},
'prieure-lichine|2019':{blend:{CS:62,ME:35,PV:3},src:'Fiche_Technique_Chateau_PRIEURE_LICHINE_MAR_RO_2019_Francais_et_Anglais.pdf',oak:40,yld:51,note:'Free of major climatic setbacks and with a very welcome episode of weather at the end of the season, the vintage was both generous and of high quality. A rollercoaster season in a vintage that was full of surprises. Following a quite mild and dry winter, the 2019 vine cycle at Château Prieuré- Lichine began with a bud-break in normal conditions at the end of March. The potential crop size was large with good, even vine shooting. The few episodes of frost experienced in the Médoc had no effect on the potential volume of the crop. Particularly rainy spring weather in April and June ensured sufﬁcient water reserves for the vines. Vine disease pressure was at a reasonable level. The ﬂowering process beneﬁted from the good weather conditions. Summer weather suddenly set in at the end of June with a heat-wave, followed by a second and more intense one, around 25th July.'},
