'lafite|1968':{blend:{CF:13,CS:57,ME:30},src:'Chateau-Lafite-Rothschild-1968.pdf',alc:11,yld:30,taste:'Beautiful brick colour with a hint of orange. Open, delicate nose with light floral notes.'},
'lafite|1975':{blend:{CF:9,CS:75,ME:16},src:'Chateau-Lafite-Rothschild-1975.pdf',alc:12.5,yld:17,taste:'On the nose the wine reveals complex and intense aromas of tobacco and black truffle. The mouth is remarkable, with a good amplitude and a lot of length, all finesse.'},
'lafite|1976':{blend:{CF:9,CS:64,ME:27},src:'Chateau-Lafite-Rothschild-1976.pdf',taste:'On the nose the wine reveals complex and intense aromas of tobacco and black truffle. The mouth is remarkable, with a good amplitude and a lot of length, all finesse.'},
'lafite|1978':{blend:{CF:11,CS:59,ME:27,PV:3},src:'Chateau-Lafite-Rothschild-1978.pdf',alc:12.5,taste:'The nose reveals notes of cedar, tobacco, and leather. Delicate and balanced, with tremendous complexity, this wine has a beautiful roundness on the palate and a long finish.'},
'lafite|1979':{blend:{CF:11,CS:66,ME:23},src:'Chateau-Lafite-Rothschild-1979.pdf',alc:12,pick:{ALL:'10-02|'},yld:34,taste:'Very expressive nose, cedar, tobacco. Fairly open and balanced at the beginning of the palate, then develops into a little thinness and a slightly acidic finish, lacking flesh.'},
'lafite|1981':{blend:{CF:11,CS:61,ME:28},src:'Chateau-Lafite-Rothschild-1981.pdf',pick:{ALL:'10-01|'},yld:35},
'lynch-bages|2018':{blend:{CF:6,CS:72,ME:19,PV:3},src:'Chateau-Lynch-Bages-2018-ENG.pdf',months:'18',oak:75,pick:{ALL:'09-19|'},note:'The second period began mid-July with fine summer weather, hot temperatures and excessive sunshine. Full flowering occurred in line with the 20-year average. Thanks to ideal weather conditions, harvest started on 19 September with the Merlot and was followed by Cabernet Sauvignon, Cabernet Franc and Petit Verdot until 9 October. Upon arrival at the cellar, the sanitary state of the grapes was perfect, with rich sugar content and exceptional polyphenols. Alcoholic fermentation was straightforward and homogeneous and average vatting time was 21 days. During the runoff from 15 to 29 October, the vats produced juice yields that were below expectations. Then came the time for malolactic fermentation, one third of which took place in vats and two thirds in barrels. It was completed in November. The first blends were carried out in December. Lynch-Bages 2018 offers a seductive mouthfeel with powerful yet silky tannins. On the palate, there is a strong prelude of black chocolate, rosemary and spices on a fresh core leading to a long finish.'},
