'rieussec|1975':{blend:{MU:2,SB:18,SEM:80},src:'Chateau-Rieussec-1975.pdf',alc:13.5,yld:14.5,taste:'This is a wine for laying down. It has all the qualities of a great sweet wine: a beautiful golden color, a nose of honey and fruit, an attack offering the wine\'s finesse without assaulting the palate, and brutally, the blossoming of its power to finish with that famous " queue de paon " given by the roast.'},
'smith-haut-lafitte|2021':{blend:{CS:60,ME:40},src:'Petit-Smith-Haut-Lafitte-Rouge-2021-EN.pdf',months:'14',oak:20,yld:22},
'smith-haut-lafitte|2025':{blend:{CF:4,CS:68,ME:27,PV:1},src:'TD-smith-haut-lafitte-2025_smith-haut-lafitte-2025-ft-gb-primeurs-pdf-1.pdf',months:'18',yld:28,taste:'The first nose reveals a beautiful freshness of ripe fruit: red berries (cherry, raspberry), black fruit (wild blackberry), and a hint of blackcurrant. With aeration, the wine unveils its tremendous aromatic potential, combining these fresh fruit notes with more delicate aromas of flowers (peony), sweet spices (fennel seed, star anise, fenugreek, mountain hay…), before revealing a darker dimension of graphite, pencil lead, and warm earth, bringing remarkable complexity. The palate opens with a surprisingly fresh attack, supported by a beautifully soft and caressing texture. The mid-palate is all finesse and delicacy at first, before expanding with restrained power and a superb structural framework. It is focused, full-bodied, dense, with impressive length and outstanding harmony. A perfectly balanced wine, marked by great precision, vibrant freshness, and remarkable energy. On the palate, one finds again the complexity revealed on the nose, with crunchy fruit, very delicate floral notes, and spices that beautifully enhance the finish.'},
